course: dictionary
lesson: 14137
title: Misadventure: bad luck and small accidents
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A misadventure is a bit of bad luck, or an unlucky accident, often a small one. It is a noun, so you can have a misadventure or several misadventures. «Our picnic was ruined by a series of small misadventures: the sandwiches blew away, then the flask spilled.» The clues show that things went wrong, but not in a very serious way.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Blew away», «spilled» and «ruined» show that the day went wrong by chance. Nobody planned it. Ask yourself: was it an accident or a choice? If something went wrong by bad luck, misadventure is a good word for it.
explain: Story writers use misadventure for funny trouble. «Toad's misadventures with motor-cars and horses» are his silly, unlucky adventures that get him into trouble. The word is not about excitement; it is about what happened to him.
explain: In British courts, the word has a special legal meaning. «Death by misadventure» is the name for a death caused by an accident during a risky activity that was still legal. Check the context: if the sentence is about a court case, use the legal meaning; if it is about a day going wrong, it means bad luck.
fact: Misadventure means a bit of bad luck or an unlucky accident, often a small one.
fact: Misadventure is a noun: a misadventure, misadventures.
fact: «Misadventures» means several unlucky events, like Toad's misadventures in the stories.
fact: In British law, «death by misadventure» means a death caused by an accident during a risky but legal activity.
exercise: «The school trip had a few misadventures: the bus broke down and the lunch boxes went missing.» What is a misadventure here? | *Bad luck and small accidents | A prize for good behaviour | A kind teacher | A long journey by plane
exercise: Mia says a misadventure is a planned adventure. What is the right meaning? | *An unlucky accident or bad luck | A planned trip to a new place | A long holiday by the sea | A type of sweet
exercise: «Toad had many misadventures before he got home.» Which word is a noun meaning unlucky events? | home | before | *misadventures | many
test: «The hikers' misadventure on the hill was caused by thick fog, and they were lost for an hour.» What is the best meaning of misadventure? | Dinner in a café | A famous painting | *An unlucky accident | A holiday rule
test: In a story, Sam's misadventures with his bike make us laugh. Why are they funny? | *Because unlucky things keep happening to him | Because he wins every race | Because they are sad and bad | Because bikes are boring
exam: In a court, a judge may say a death was «by misadventure» when an accident happened during a risky but legal activity. What does this legal sense mean? | *A death caused by an accident during a risky but legal activity | A death that was a crime | A death that was planned by the victim | A death that nobody reported
